# now-playing shellcheck config. POSIX-dash mode: `shellcheck -s dash <file>`,
# which test/lint.t runs over every shell file in the repo.
#
# Only findings that are WRONG HERE FOR A STRUCTURAL REASON are disabled
# repo-wide. Anything that is merely inconvenient gets FIXED instead: the four
# `A && B || C` notes (SC2015) in setup.sh were restructured into if/else rather
# than silenced, because the warning is correct in general and suppressing it
# would leave the trap armed for the next edit. Genuinely one-off cases carry an
# inline `# shellcheck disable=` with a reason beside the code (np-ctl's
# deliberate single quotes, harness_lib's externally-consumed HERE).
#
# SC1091: every test sources the harness by a COMPUTED path, `. "$(dirname
# "$0")/harness_lib"`, which shellcheck cannot resolve statically. Nothing is
# lost by not following it: test/lint.t lints harness_lib DIRECTLY, so the file
# is checked, just not through the seven call sites. Following it instead
# (external-sources + source-path=SCRIPTDIR) was tried and is a lateral move --
# it trades seven harmless SC1091 notes for seven harmless SC2119 notes about
# bare `pass` inheriting the script's positional parameters.
#
# SC1007: the `CDPATH= cd` idiom, used by every self-locating script here to
# neutralise CDPATH for exactly one command. shellcheck reads the empty
# assignment as a suspected typo; it is the correct portable spelling.
disable=SC1091,SC1007
